# 3. Project Vision

The long-term vision of VORTEX is to create a robotic platform that can physically interact with people and its environment while remaining based on understandable embedded-system principles.

The robot is envisioned as a system that can:

* Listen to predefined voice commands
* Move through a physical environment
* Detect nearby obstacles
* Monitor environmental conditions
* Control connected home appliances
* Provide visual feedback
* Provide audio feedback
* Communicate through IoT infrastructure
* React according to programmed logic
* Support future hardware modules

The ultimate objective is to continuously evolve the VORTEX platform through successive hardware and software generations.

---

# 4. Core Concept

The central concept behind VORTEX 2.0 is:

> **A robot can be interactive without depending on AI.**

VORTEX uses a deterministic control architecture.

Instead of:

```text
User
 ↓
AI Model
 ↓
Generated Response
 ↓
Action
```

VORTEX follows:

```text
User
 ↓
Voice Command
 ↓
Command Recognition
 ↓
Predefined Logic
 ↓
Controller
 ↓
Action
 ↓
Feedback
```

This architecture allows the behavior of the robot to be explicitly programmed and understood.

