# 9. Voice Interaction

Voice interaction is one of the primary human interfaces of VORTEX 2.0.

A **VC-02 voice-recognition module** is used to detect predefined commands.

A typical interaction sequence is:

```text
User
 ↓
"Hey Vortex"
 ↓
Voice Module
 ↓
ESP32
 ↓
Command Processing
 ↓
Action
 ↓
Audio / OLED Feedback
```

Example commands include:

### Movement

```text
Forward
Backward
Left
Right
Stop
```

### Appliances

```text
Fan ON
Fan OFF

Light ON
Light OFF

Water Motor ON
Water Motor OFF

TV ON
TV OFF
```

The command vocabulary can be expanded or modified as the firmware develops.

---

# 10. Environmental Awareness

VORTEX uses sensors to obtain information about its environment.

### Ultrasonic Sensing

The HC-SR04 can be used for:

* Distance measurement
* Obstacle detection
* Front-facing environmental awareness

### Environmental Monitoring

The DHT22 provides:

* Temperature
* Humidity

The sensor information can be displayed through the OLED interface or used by the control logic.

---

# 11. Robotic Movement

VORTEX 2.0 uses a motor-driven mobile platform.

An **L298N motor driver** interfaces the ESP32 with the DC gear motors.

Basic movement functions include:

```text
FORWARD
BACKWARD
LEFT
RIGHT
STOP
```

Movement commands are processed by the ESP32 and translated into motor-control signals.

Obstacle information from the ultrasonic sensor can also be incorporated into movement decisions.

---

# 12. Visual Interaction

An **SSD1306 OLED display** forms part of the robot's visual interface.

The display can communicate the robot's current state to the user.

Possible display states include:

```text
SYSTEM STARTING

SYSTEM AWAKE

LISTENING...

MOVING FORWARD

OBSTACLE DETECTED

FAN ON

LIGHT OFF

SYSTEM IDLE
```

The VORTEX 2.0 concept also includes expressive OLED graphics that can give the robot a recognizable visual identity.

---

# 13. Audio Interaction

A **DFPlayer Mini** provides audio playback functionality.

An external speaker can be used for system responses.

The startup sequence can include:

```text
BOOT
 ↓
INITIALIZATION
 ↓
SYSTEM CHECK
 ↓
VORTEX ONLINE
 ↓
"Hi Buddy, How can I help you?"
```

Pre-recorded audio can also provide feedback for commands and system events.

